Description: antinomie: record the completion of an io_uring IOPOLL request
 A ring set up with IORING_SETUP_IOPOLL completes its reads and writes
 in io_do_iopoll(): the completed requests are cut from the poll list
 and posted by __io_submit_flush_completions(), which does not pass
 through io_req_complete_defer(), where the recorder's completion hook
 sits. The recorder never saw the completion, and when the request was
 freed it was recorded as ABANDONED with no result. io_complete_rw_iopoll()
 captured the data, so only the completion record was missing.
 .
 - io_do_iopoll() calls ant_uring_complete() for each completed request,
   with the result and flags the CQE gets, before the flush posts it.
 .
 Found by the 0.9.0 bug hunt (K1-08e). No contract change (revision
 22).
Author: MikiMiku <jonathanirvinjo@gmail.com>
Origin: project
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-22

---
diff --git a/io_uring/rw.c b/io_uring/rw.c
index 848cc40ce..ce3fdd7bc 100644
--- a/io_uring/rw.c
+++ b/io_uring/rw.c
@@ -1246,6 +1246,10 @@ int io_do_iopoll(struct io_ring_ctx *ctx, bool force_nonspin)
 			break;
 		nr_events++;
 		req->cqe.flags = io_put_kbuf(req, req->cqe.res, NULL);
+		/* Posted by __io_submit_flush_completions() below, which skips
+		 * io_req_complete_defer(): the recorder's completion is here.
+		 */
+		ant_uring_complete(req, req->cqe.res, req->cqe.flags, true);
 		if (req->opcode != IORING_OP_URING_CMD)
 			io_req_rw_cleanup(req, 0);
 	}
